## Part S: single chunks on the device (K = 32)

Each row: one operand pair, block shape and variant, every kind of input (README), two draws each. With one chunk the partial values are the accumulator and the device's result, so each element is checked against the step bound with no model, at the smallest M_j (the larger of |acc| and the chunk's largest lifted product). `new`: the error over the new facts' bound (the minimum of the two arms); `loss arm`: over the second arm alone, kappa A_j + rho2 M_j + sigma |s + c| + alpha; `round 24`: over the round-24 facts' bound; `magnitude`: elements whose result exceeds |acc| + sum |a b|.

