## Part B: every K that compiles

Each row: one operand pair, block shape and K, every kind of input, one draw each. `interval`: the largest error over the half-width (on its side) of the interval the facts imply (`new`, and `round 24` for the round-24 facts); `chunk`: on wgmma, the largest error of one chunk of the model's chain over the new step bound; `half-width`: the smallest ratio of the new composed bound to the round-24 one; `model = device`: elements whose device result equals the model's, bit for bit (wgmma).

