## Part C: chains of tl.dot(p, v, acc) (tutorial 06)

`for t in range(T): [acc = acc * alpha_t]; acc = tl.dot(p_t.to(fp8), v_t, acc)`, p_t [M, 64] converted in registers, v_t [64, N], every acc_t stored. `per dot`: each dot from the stored accumulator before it (times alpha_t in float32) against the new facts' interval (and, on wgmma, the model, and each chunk of the model's chain against the new step bound). `whole chain` (no rescale): the final result against the facts composed over all 2T chunks from the initial accumulator; `half-width`: that composed bound, new over round 24, for the element where the ratio is largest (`max`) and smallest (`min`). Inputs: `softmax` (p = exp2 of random scores minus the row maximum, v = randn), `accdom` (after a randn * 2^6 accumulator, products just below the accumulator's window unit), `subwin` (num-dot-chunk's window case).

