## Totals

Part S: single chunks (the step bound on the device's own values); Part B: every K; Part C: chains, per dot and whole. `new`: the largest error over the new facts' bound (step bound in Part S, interval otherwise); `loss arm`: the step over the second arm alone (Part S: the device's step; Parts B and C: each chunk of the model's chain, wgmma); `round 24`: as `new` against the round-24 facts; `chunk`: each chunk of the model's chain over the new step bound (wgmma); `half-width`: the smallest ratio of the new composed bound to the round-24 one; `magnitude`: results above |acc| + sum |a b|.

